.TH DAGDA-MIGRATE 1 2026-11-13 Dagda "Dagda tools"
.SH NAME
dagda-migrate \- move a Macha node's store from layout v18 to v19 in place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dagda-migrate
.B \-\-state
.I DIR
.B \-\-node-state
.I DIR
.B \-\-cluster-key
.I FILE
.I KEY
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR DIR ]...
.RB [ \-\-control
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-cache
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-heads ]
.RB [ \-\-space
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-\-reverse ]
.br
.B dagda-migrate
.B \-\-state
.I DIR
.B \-\-node-state
.I DIR
.B \-\-cluster-key
.I FILE
.I KEY
.RB [ \-\-backend
.IR DIR ]...
.RB [ \-\-control
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-cache
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-space
.IR NAME ]
.B \-\-write-manifest
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-resume ]
.br
.B dagda-migrate
.B \-\-compare-before
.I FILE
.B \-\-compare-after
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-expect-before
.IR 18 ]
.RB [ \-\-expect-after
.IR 19 ]
.br
.B dagda-migrate
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dagda-migrate
moves a node's layout v18 state and disks, Macha's, to Dagda's layout v19 in
place, with the node stopped. It is the only way a v18 disk becomes v19: the
store refuses one at open. It does not need twice the storage, and an
interrupted run is finished by running it again.
.PP
The manifest form reads the whole state and writes nothing under it: run it
once before the migration and once after, then compare the two. The compare
form reports every difference by name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-state " DIR"
Dagda's state directory: the storage-layout marker, the ledgers and the
control store.
.TP
.BI \-\-node-state " DIR"
Dannan's state directory, where the node's key custody lives.
.TP
.BI \-\-cluster-key " FILE"
The cluster key file.
.TP
.I KEY
Opens the node's custody:
.BI \-\-passphrase-env " VAR"
for the passphrase in that environment variable, or
.BI \-\-credential " NAME"
with an optional
.BI \-\-credentials-dir " DIR" \fR,
as the node takes it.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " DIR"
Each DATA backend's path as the node's configuration names it; repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-control " DIR"
The control store's path, when it is not
.IR STATE /metadata-objects.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache " DIR"
The persistent cache's path, if the node has one.
.TP
.B \-\-heads
Also moves Macha's metadata and the cache seed to the heads' layout. On a
state already at v19 it runs that pass alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-space " NAME"
The head space;
.B macha/namespace
unless given.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Classifies and reports, and writes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Goes back from v19 to v18, the metadata included, so the node can return to
Macha 0.93.
.TP
.BI \-\-write-manifest " FILE"
Writes the state's manifest to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Continues a manifest pass from its partial. It is refused while another pass
is writing that partial.
.TP
.BI \-\-compare-before " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-compare-after " FILE
The two manifests to compare.
.TP
.BI \-\-expect-before " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-expect-after " N
The layouts the two manifests must record; 18 and 19 unless given.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Migrating: 0 when the state is v19, migrated now or already; 1 when refused or
failed, the reason on standard error; 2 for a usage error.
.PP
Writing a manifest: 0 when the manifest is whole, which says nothing of what is
in it.
.PP
Comparing: 0 only when nothing differs and everything was checked; 1 for any
difference, anything not checked, or a manifest that is not whole.
